-- Hardcoded monster levels. Everything that needs the level of a monster (daily contracts, prey, rewarded creatures...) reads it from here
-- (MonsterLevel.get in data/lib/301-monsterlevel.lua). To balance a monster, change its number. Names in lower case.
--
-- The numbers were generated with the formula of data/lib/301-monsterlevel.lua (health and damage of the attacks: average and burst):
--     offense = damage/s * 10 * 0.6 + burst * 0.4,  level = floor(sqrt(health * offense) ^ 0.655 * 0.61)
-- The comment of each line shows the data used: health | experience | damage per second | burst.
-- A monster that is not in this table (a new monster) gets its level calculated by the formula, so it still works; use /monsterlevels
-- (staff) to list the monsters missing here with the lines ready to paste.
-- Lines marked with CHECK have no damage information (no attack, or attacks by script without min/max): the level came from the experience.

